      "writtenOn": "2018-02-26T19:45:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "while this may look like good defensive coding, it has the potential to hide bugs. There is at least one other place in the code where we rely on the value being either within range (enforced here: https://cs.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/base/telephony/java/android/telephony/SignalStrength.java?q\u003dSignalStrength.java\u0026sq\u003dpackage:android\u0026dr\u0026l\u003d327) or INVALID.\n\ntl;dr, if the value gets here, we should explicitly check for \u003d\u003d INVALID and be done with it (just like we do for the getAsuLevel() function), or if we really want to triple check ourselves, there should be two checks... one for INVALID (normal) and a nasty Log.WTF() for value !\u003d invalid \u0026\u0026 value \u003e MAX. I submit that the latter is overkill, and we should just check for invalid.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 751,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 752,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "23b59e8d814ea64066577b4e396f910a9c9209d5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
